            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "quirks": [
    "One node, two endpoints. The output field \"mode\" names the one that ran so nobody infers it from the shape of next_cursor.",
    "Batch read returns every id asked for in one answer, so its next_cursor is always null. Only list mode pages.",
    "More than 100 ids is cut into 100-id calls and fanned out under the app rate limits.",
    "An id HubSpot cannot read (archived, deleted, never there) comes back in \"errors\" with HTTP 207. It does not fail the call.",
    "id_property reads records by a unique property such as email instead of the record id."
  ]
}
